  "label": "Madame Tussauds Hollywood",
  "description": "Madame Tussauds is a global chain of wax museums known for creating lifelike wax figures of celebrities, historical figures, and fictional characters. The presence of the wax figure in a branded setting (Madame Tussauds Hollywood) situates the image within a commercial, tourist-oriented context, which contrasts with the emotionally heavy message. This juxtaposition may be interpreted as ironic or symbolic — using a place of entertainment to deliver a warning about emotional pain.",
